WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.436
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR: At a
nondescript storefront in Kyiv,

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:06.072
covered with plastic
against prying eyes,

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.574
a major war effort is underway.

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:09.442
ANDRII KOLESNYK: Oh.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:10.676
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
Boxes of kit

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.181
reveal a first of its kind,
fatigues designed for a mother

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.382
to be.

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:18.418
So was there never, Andrii,
anything for pregnant women

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.218
before?

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:20.186
ANDRII KOLESNYK: Never, ever.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:21.854
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
Now many pregnant women

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:23.056
are fighting the Russians?

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.858
- I'm not sure that
a lot, but there are.

00:00:25.891 --> 00:00:27.126
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
Andrii and Ksenia

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:31.397
are married TV journalists in
real life who now do this work.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.833
A female friend turned
frontline sniper

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:37.503
told them that she was pregnant
and needed a new uniform.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.739
They're also sending
female soldiers

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:44.444
smaller boots, lighter Kevlar
plates for their flak vests.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:48.548
On this day, Roksolana
comes in for a new uniform.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.250
She's in an intelligence
unit near the front

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:54.220
and joined up in March
totally unprepared.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:55.455
- [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.689
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
It's so valuable

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:59.025
to have these people who
understand that we are

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:02.195
tired of wearing clothes
that are three sizes too big,

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.196
she tells me.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:06.065
We had no helmets, we
had old flak jackets,

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:08.167
we wore tracksuits and sneakers.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.504
Now we feel that we're humans.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.206
The Ukrainian
Ministry of Defense

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.441
says that are more
than 50,000 women

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:19.378
under arms, more than 5,000
of them on the front line.

00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:21.814
Amongst them, Andrei's sister.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:25.885 line:0%
ANDRII KOLESNYK: She received
men's uniform, men's underwear,

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:28.754 line:0%
everything that
designed for men.

00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:29.555
30, 35--

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:30.723
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
Females also

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.159
need customized
sanitary, medical,

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.094
and humanitarian supplies.

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:39.599
Ksenia and Andrii have sent out
3,000 of these care packages,

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:43.269
they've produced 300 uniforms
and planned for at least

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:47.673
another 2,000, all winterized.

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:52.145
And then there's
this vital tool.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.679 line:0%
Oh my God.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:55.214 line:0%
I've never seen that.

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:59.252 line:0%
A feminine urinary director
for women of all ages.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.386 line:0%
ANDRII KOLESNYK: Well--

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.354 line:0%
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR: Basically,
they pee in that, right,

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.221 line:0%
if there's no toilet?

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:03.022 line:0%
ANDRII KOLESNYK: Not in.

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:04.223 line:0%
They pee like men.

00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:05.458
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
Look at that.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:06.726
Oh my God.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.295
If only I'd known that in all
the years I was in the field.

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.063
And as a parting
gift, they throw

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:13.266
in this book on
resilience and courage

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.401
amid battle and in captivity--

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:16.669
- [NON-ENGLISH SINGING]

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:20.006
Which happened to Elina
Panina five months

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.942
ago after the fall of Mariupol.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.645
She is part of a canine
border guard unit.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.314
And like so many of the
port city's defenders,

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:32.885
she'd been hunkering down in
the giant Azovstal steel plant.

00:02:32.918 --> 00:02:36.389
She was recently released as
part of an all-female prisoner

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.457
exchange with Russia.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.727
We meet at this pizza
bar run by vets.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.431
Were you prepared
for life as a POW?

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:46.699
- [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:48.534
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR:
No I was not, she says.

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:51.437
And we discuss this a lot with
the other women prisoners,

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.507
that life hasn't trained
us for such an ordeal.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:58.077
While in captivity though, I
said, I'll continue my service.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.813
And I have no plans to stop.

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:02.982
Back at their private
procurement center,

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:05.351
Andrii says he
wishes he could join

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:07.987
his sister, father,
and brother-in-law

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.188
all at the front.

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:12.491
But a physical disability
means that he's not eligible.

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:14.293 line:0%
ANDRII KOLESNYK: For
a man, it's kind of

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:17.563 line:0%
hard to understand
that you can't go there

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:20.233 line:0%
and your sister is there.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:25.705 line:0%
So I'm trying to do my
best here to help not only

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.807 line:0%
my family, but the whole army.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.675
- [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:31.577
CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR: And the
reviews from the battlefield

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.812
are in.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.581
It's just amazing,
says Anastasia.

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:37.149
I'm happy as a child.

00:03:37.182 --> 00:03:39.719
The uniform is ideal,
it looks great,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.488
and the fabric is very sturdy.

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:45.958
Meantime, Roksolana's new
boots are made for marching

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:48.127
all the way back to the front.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.997
Christiane Amanpour, CNN Kyiv.

